// NOTE: This entire module was generated by an LLM (Gemini) as a pure-Rust port of
// ICU4C's `UMutableCPTrie` (`icu4c/source/common/umutablecptrie.cpp`), replacing the
// former `icu_codepointtrie_builder` crate's Wasm (`wasmi`) and native ICU4C FFI
// backends.
//
// Summary of implementation design and reasoning:
//
// 1. Why a direct algorithmic port of `umutablecptrie.cpp`:
//    ICU4X's `CodePointTrie` runtime representation (`CodePointTrieHeader`, multi-stage
//    `index` array, and `data` array with trailing `high_value` and `error_value`) is
//    defined by ICU4C's `UCPTrie` binary format. Producing tries that are not merely
//    functionally equivalent, but bit-for-bit identical to ICU4C across `TrieType::Fast`
//    and `TrieType::Small` and all value widths (8, 16, and 32-bit), requires following
//    the exact same compaction heuristics, block deduplication order, overlap searches,
//    null-block selection, and padding rules as `umutablecptrie_buildImmutable`.
//
// 2. Core data structures:
//    - `MutableCodePointTrie`: Mirrors ICU4C's `UMutableCPTrie`. The Unicode code point
//      space (`0..0x110000`) is partitioned into 16-code-point small data blocks
//      (`UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3 = 4`, `I_LIMIT = 0x11000` blocks). Each block has an entry in
//      `flags` (`ALL_SAME`, `MIXED`, or `SAME_AS`) and `index`:
//        * `ALL_SAME`: `index[i]` stores the uniform 32-bit data value directly without
//          allocating space in `data`.
//        * `MIXED`: `index[i]` stores the starting offset of a block in `data`. In the
//          BMP (`i < BMP_I_LIMIT`), `get_data_block` allocates 64-entry fast blocks
//          (4 consecutive 16-entry small blocks) at once to match fast-index granularity.
//        * `SAME_AS`: Used during compaction to point to an earlier identical `ALL_SAME`
//          block index.
//    - `AllSameBlocks`: A 32-entry frequency table (`AllSameBlockEntry`) used during
//      `compact_whole_data_blocks` to deduplicate `ALL_SAME` blocks and track reference
//      counts so the most-referenced uniform block can be chosen as `data_null_offset`
//      (which accelerates range iteration in `CodePointTrie`). If more than 32 distinct
//      uniform block values exist, it falls back to scanning earlier blocks and evicts
//      the least-used entry, matching ICU4C.
//    - `MixedBlocks`: An open-addressed hash table over sliding windows of length
//      `block_length` in the compacted data or index arrays. Each 32-bit table entry
//      packs the upper hash bits (`hash_code << shift`) with a 1-based array offset in
//      the low `mask` bits (reserving `0` for empty slots). Used to find exact block
//      matches in O(1) expected time before falling back to bounded suffix-prefix
//      overlap checks (`get_overlap` / `get_all_same_overlap`).
//    - `BlockElem`: A small internal trait implemented for `u16` and `u32` so that
//      `equal_blocks`, `get_overlap`, and `MixedBlocks` can operate generically across
//      both 32-bit data blocks and 16-bit index blocks without C++ `void *` casts or
//      duplicated code.
//
// 3. Compaction pipeline (`compact_trie` and `build`):
//    - Compile-time width check & masking: `CodePointTrie` only supports 1..=4 byte
//      `TrieValue::ULE` types, enforced at monomorphization time via
//      `const { assert!(matches!(size_of::<T::ULE>(), 1..=4)); }`. For 1-byte and 2-byte
//      types, `mask_values` masks stored 32-bit values to 8 or 16 bits before compaction
//      so values that become equal after truncation can be deduplicated.
//    - `high_start` computation: Scans downward from `high_start` to find the lowest
//      code point above which all values equal `high_value` (the value at `U+10FFFF`),
//      rounded up to a 512-code-point (`UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY`) boundary and
//      pinned to at least the fast-index limit (`0x10000` for `Fast`, `0x1000` for `Small`).
//    - ASCII capture & whole-block pass (`compact_whole_data_blocks`): The linear ASCII
//      prefix (`0..0x80`) is read via `self.get(c)` *before* `compact_whole_data_blocks`
//      runs, because `compact_whole_data_blocks` mutates `flags[i]` to `SAME_AS` and
//      overwrites `index[i]` with block indices (which `self.get()` would misinterpret
//      as `MIXED` data offsets). `compact_whole_data_blocks` also demotes `MIXED` blocks
//      whose elements are all identical back to `ALL_SAME`, and promotes non-uniform
//      4-sub-block fast blocks from `ALL_SAME` to `MIXED`.
//    - Data compaction (`compact_data`): Populates `new_data` starting with the linear
//      ASCII block, then compacts fast-range blocks (length 64) and small-range blocks
//      (length 16) using `MixedBlocks` for full matches and `get_overlap` /
//      `get_all_same_overlap` for partial overlaps. A small-range null block is prevented
//      from aliasing the start of a fast block (`is_start_of_some_fast_block`) as required
//      by ICU4C's range-iteration logic.
//    - Index compaction (`compact_index`): When `high_start` is within the fast range,
//      the index is simply the flat 16-bit fast index. Otherwise, condenses the fast
//      index, classifies supplementary index-3 blocks (`I3_NULL`, `I3_BMP`, `I3_16`,
//      `I3_18`), encodes 18-bit index-3 blocks (packing every 8 18-bit data offsets into
//      9 `u16` words with the upper 2-bit pairs collected into the leading `u16`),
//      compacts index-3 blocks with overlap, and finally compacts index-2 blocks while
//      writing the index-1 table.
//    - Alignment and trailer values: Pads `index16` to an even length when elements are
//      >2 bytes, and appends `high_value` and `error_value` at the end of `data` (with
//      padding so total byte length is a multiple of 4, matching ICU4C's layout).
//
// 4. Rust idioms & ICU4X lint compliance:
//    - `icu_collections` enforces `#![deny(clippy::indexing_slicing, clippy::unwrap_used,
//      clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic)]` and forbids `unsafe`.
//    - Rather than suppressing `clippy::indexing_slicing` across the port, all C array
//      indexing and pointer arithmetic was translated to checked slice access (`.get()`,
//      `.get_mut()`), slice bulk operations (`.fill()`, `.copy_from_slice()`,
//      `.copy_within()`, `.ends_with()`, `.last()`), and fixed-size chunk iterators
//      (`.as_chunks::<8>()` / `.as_chunks_mut::<9>()` for the 18-bit index-3 packing
//      and `.as_chunks_mut::<SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK>()` for condensing the
//      fast index).
//    - The only two `#[expect(clippy::unwrap_used)]` annotations are at the final
//      construction step in `MutableCodePointTrie::build`, where `T::try_from_u32`
//      round-trips values that originated from `T::to_u32` and `CodePointTrie::try_new`
//      validates the freshly built header, index, and data vectors.
//    - Output was verified bit-for-bit against ICU4C's `UMutableCPTrie` (via Wasm) and
//      all existing TOML round-trip tests in `tests/cpt.rs`.

use super::CodePointTrie;
use super::CodePointTrieHeader;
use super::TrieType;
use super::TrieValue;
use alloc::{vec, vec::Vec};
use core::ops::RangeInclusive;
use zerovec::ZeroVec;

/// Builder for a [`CodePointTrie`].
#[allow(clippy::exhaustive_structs)]
#[derive(Debug)]
pub struct CodePointTrieBuilder<T: TrieValue> {
    inner: MutableCodePointTrie,
    trie_type: TrieType,
    default_value: T,
}

impl<T: TrieValue> CodePointTrieBuilder<T> {
    /// Creates a new [`CodePointTrieBuilder`] with the given defaults.
    pub fn new(default_value: T, error_value: T, trie_type: TrieType) -> Self {
        const {
            assert!(matches!(size_of::<T::ULE>(), 1..=4));
        }
        Self {
            inner: MutableCodePointTrie::new(default_value.to_u32(), error_value.to_u32()),
            trie_type,
            default_value,
        }
    }

    /// Sets a value for a codepoint.
    pub fn set_value(&mut self, cp: u32, value: T) {
        if value == self.default_value || cp > char::MAX as u32 {
            return;
        }
        self.inner.set(cp, value.to_u32());
    }

    /// Adds a set of codepoints with the same value.
    pub fn set_range_value(&mut self, cps: RangeInclusive<u32>, value: T) {
        if value == self.default_value {
            return;
        }
        self.inner.set_range(
            (*cps.start()).min(char::MAX as u32),
            (*cps.end()).min(char::MAX as u32),
            value.to_u32(),
        );
    }

    /// Build the [`CodePointTrie`].
    pub fn build(self) -> CodePointTrie<'static, T> {
        self.inner.build(self.trie_type)
    }
}

const MAX_UNICODE: u32 = 0x10ffff;
const UNICODE_LIMIT: usize = 0x110000;
const BMP_LIMIT: usize = 0x10000;
const ASCII_LIMIT: usize = 0x80;

const UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT: usize = 6;
const UCPTRIE_FAST_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH: usize = 1 << UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT;

const UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3: usize = 4;
const UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2: usize = 5 + UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
const UCPTRIE_SHIFT_1: usize = 5 + UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2;
const UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2_3: usize = UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2 - UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
const UCPTRIE_SHIFT_1_2: usize = UCPTRIE_SHIFT_1 - UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2;

const UCPTRIE_SMALL_LIMIT: usize = 0x1000;
const UCPTRIE_BMP_INDEX_LENGTH: usize = 0x10000 >> UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT;

const UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_BLOCK_LENGTH: usize = 1 << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_1_2;
const UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_MASK: usize = UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_BLOCK_LENGTH - 1;
const UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY: usize = 1 << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2;
const UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH: usize = 1 << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2_3;
const UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH: usize = 1 << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
const UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK: usize = UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH - 1;

const UCPTRIE_NO_INDEX3_NULL_OFFSET: i32 = 0x7fff;
const UCPTRIE_NO_DATA_NULL_OFFSET: i32 = 0xfffff;

const I_LIMIT: usize = UNICODE_LIMIT >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
const BMP_I_LIMIT: usize = BMP_LIMIT >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
const ASCII_I_LIMIT: usize = ASCII_LIMIT >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;

const SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK: usize = 1 << (UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT - UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);

// Flag values for data blocks.
const ALL_SAME: u8 = 0;
const MIXED: u8 = 1;
const SAME_AS: u8 = 2;

const INITIAL_DATA_LENGTH: usize = 1 << 14;

// Flag values for index-3 blocks while compacting/building.
const I3_NULL: u8 = 0;
const I3_BMP: u8 = 1;
const I3_16: u8 = 2;
const I3_18: u8 = 3;

const INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH: usize =
    UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH + UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH / 8;

trait BlockElem: Copy {
    fn to_u32(self) -> u32;
}

impl BlockElem for u16 {
    #[inline]
    fn to_u32(self) -> u32 {
        self as u32
    }
}

impl BlockElem for u32 {
    #[inline]
    fn to_u32(self) -> u32 {
        self
    }
}

#[inline]
fn equal_blocks<A: BlockElem, B: BlockElem>(s: &[A], t: &[B], length: usize) -> bool {
    s.iter()
        .zip(t)
        .take(length)
        .all(|(a, b)| a.to_u32() == b.to_u32())
}

#[inline]
fn all_values_same_as(p: &[u32], length: usize, value: u32) -> bool {
    p.iter().take(length).all(|&x| x == value)
}

/// Search for an identical block.
fn find_same_block(
    p: &[u16],
    mut p_start: usize,
    length: usize,
    q: &[u16],
    q_start: usize,
    block_length: usize,
) -> Option<usize> {
    let length = length.checked_sub(block_length)?;
    let q_slice = q.get(q_start..)?;
    while p_start <= length {
        if equal_blocks(p.get(p_start..)?, q_slice, block_length) {
            return Some(p_start);
        }
        p_start += 1;
    }
    None
}

fn find_all_same_block(
    p: &[u32],
    start: usize,
    limit: usize,
    value: u32,
    block_length: usize,
) -> Option<usize> {
    let limit = limit.checked_sub(block_length)?;
    let mut block = start;
    while block <= limit {
        if p.get(block) == Some(&value) {
            let mut i = 1;
            loop {
                if i == block_length {
                    return Some(block);
                }
                if p.get(block + i) != Some(&value) {
                    block += i;
                    break;
                }
                i += 1;
            }
        }
        block += 1;
    }
    None
}

/// Look for maximum overlap of the beginning of the other block
/// with the previous, adjacent block.
fn get_overlap<A: BlockElem, B: BlockElem>(
    p: &[A],
    length: usize,
    q: &[B],
    q_start: usize,
    block_length: usize,
) -> usize {
    let mut overlap = block_length - 1;
    debug_assert!(overlap <= length);
    let q_slice = q.get(q_start..).unwrap_or(&[]);
    while overlap > 0
        && !equal_blocks(
            p.get(length.saturating_sub(overlap)..).unwrap_or(&[]),
            q_slice,
            overlap,
        )
    {
        overlap -= 1;
    }
    overlap
}

fn get_all_same_overlap(p: &[u32], length: usize, value: u32, block_length: usize) -> usize {
    let min = length.saturating_sub(block_length - 1);
    let mut i = length;
    while min < i && p.get(i - 1) == Some(&value) {
        i -= 1;
    }
    length - i
}

fn is_start_of_some_fast_block(data_offset: u32, index: &[u32], fast_i_limit: usize) -> bool {
    index
        .iter()
        .take(fast_i_limit)
        .step_by(SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK)
        .any(|&x| x == data_offset)
}

#[derive(Copy, Clone, Default)]
struct AllSameBlockEntry {
    index: usize,
    value: u32,
    ref_count: usize,
}

struct AllSameBlocks {
    length: usize,
    most_recent: Option<usize>,
    entries: [AllSameBlockEntry; Self::CAPACITY],
}

enum FindOrAddResult {
    Found(usize),
    NewUnique,
    Overflow,
}

impl AllSameBlocks {
    const CAPACITY: usize = 32;

    fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            length: 0,
            most_recent: None,
            entries: [AllSameBlockEntry::default(); Self::CAPACITY],
        }
    }

    fn find_or_add(&mut self, index: usize, count: usize, value: u32) -> FindOrAddResult {
        if let Some(mr) = self.most_recent
            && let Some(entry) = self.entries.get_mut(mr)
            && entry.value == value
        {
            entry.ref_count += count;
            return FindOrAddResult::Found(entry.index);
        }
        for (i, entry) in self.entries.iter_mut().take(self.length).enumerate() {
            if entry.value == value {
                self.most_recent = Some(i);
                entry.ref_count += count;
                return FindOrAddResult::Found(entry.index);
            }
        }
        let idx = self.length;
        if let Some(entry) = self.entries.get_mut(idx) {
            self.most_recent = Some(idx);
            *entry = AllSameBlockEntry {
                index,
                value,
                ref_count: count,
            };
            self.length += 1;
            FindOrAddResult::NewUnique
        } else {
            FindOrAddResult::Overflow
        }
    }

    /// Replaces the block which has the lowest reference count.
    fn add(&mut self, index: usize, count: usize, value: u32) {
        debug_assert_eq!(self.length, Self::CAPACITY);
        let mut least = 0;
        let mut least_count = I_LIMIT;
        for (i, entry) in self.entries.iter().take(self.length).enumerate() {
            debug_assert_ne!(entry.value, value);
            if entry.ref_count < least_count {
                least = i;
                least_count = entry.ref_count;
            }
        }
        self.most_recent = Some(least);
        if let Some(entry) = self.entries.get_mut(least) {
            *entry = AllSameBlockEntry {
                index,
                value,
                ref_count: count,
            };
        }
    }

    fn find_most_used(&self) -> Option<usize> {
        let mut max_index = None;
        let mut max_count = 0;
        for entry in self.entries.iter().take(self.length) {
            if entry.ref_count > max_count {
                max_index = Some(entry.index);
                max_count = entry.ref_count;
            }
        }
        max_index
    }
}

/// Custom hash table for mixed-value blocks to be found anywhere in the
/// compacted data or index so far.
struct MixedBlocks {
    table: Vec<u32>,
    length: usize,
    shift: u32,
    mask: u32,
    block_length: usize,
}

impl MixedBlocks {
    fn new() -> Self {
        Self {
            table: Vec::new(),
            length: 0,
            shift: 0,
            mask: 0,
            block_length: 0,
        }
    }

    fn init(&mut self, max_length: usize, new_block_length: usize) {
        // We store actual data indexes + 1 to reserve 0 for empty entries.
        let max_data_index = max_length.saturating_sub(new_block_length) + 1;
        let new_length;
        if max_data_index <= 0xfff {
            // 4k
            new_length = 6007;
            self.shift = 12;
            self.mask = 0xfff;
        } else if max_data_index <= 0x7fff {
            // 32k
            new_length = 50021;
            self.shift = 15;
            self.mask = 0x7fff;
        } else if max_data_index <= 0x1ffff {
            // 128k
            new_length = 200003;
            self.shift = 17;
            self.mask = 0x1ffff;
        } else {
            // maxDataIndex up to around MAX_DATA_LENGTH, ca. 1.1M
            new_length = 1500007;
            self.shift = 21;
            self.mask = 0x1fffff;
        }
        self.table.clear();
        self.table.resize(new_length, 0);
        self.length = new_length;
        self.block_length = new_block_length;
    }

    fn extend<T: BlockElem>(
        &mut self,
        data: &[T],
        min_start: usize,
        prev_data_length: usize,
        new_data_length: usize,
    ) {
        let mut start = if prev_data_length >= self.block_length {
            let s = prev_data_length - self.block_length;
            if s >= min_start {
                s + 1 // Skip the last block that we added last time.
            } else {
                min_start // Begin with the first full block.
            }
        } else {
            min_start
        };
        if new_data_length >= self.block_length {
            let end = new_data_length - self.block_length;
            while start <= end {
                let hash_code = self.make_hash_code(data, start);
                self.add_entry(data, start, hash_code, start);
                start += 1;
            }
        }
    }

    fn find_block<A: BlockElem, B: BlockElem>(
        &self,
        data: &[A],
        block_data: &[B],
        block_start: usize,
    ) -> Option<usize> {
        let hash_code = self.make_hash_code(block_data, block_start);
        let entry_index = self
            .find_entry(data, block_data, block_start, hash_code)
            .ok()?;
        let entry = *self.table.get(entry_index)?;
        Some(((entry & self.mask) - 1) as usize)
    }

    fn find_all_same_block(&self, data: &[u32], block_value: u32) -> Option<usize> {
        let hash_code = self.make_hash_code_value(block_value);
        let entry_index = self.find_entry_value(data, block_value, hash_code).ok()?;
        let entry = *self.table.get(entry_index)?;
        Some(((entry & self.mask) - 1) as usize)
    }

    fn make_hash_code<T: BlockElem>(&self, block_data: &[T], block_start: usize) -> u32 {
        let mut iter = block_data.iter().skip(block_start).take(self.block_length);
        let Some(first) = iter.next() else {
            return 0;
        };
        let mut hash_code = first.to_u32();
        for elem in iter {
            hash_code = hash_code.wrapping_mul(37).wrapping_add(elem.to_u32());
        }
        hash_code
    }

    fn make_hash_code_value(&self, block_value: u32) -> u32 {
        let mut hash_code = block_value;
        for _ in 1..self.block_length {
            hash_code = hash_code.wrapping_mul(37).wrapping_add(block_value);
        }
        hash_code
    }

    fn add_entry<T: BlockElem>(
        &mut self,
        data: &[T],
        block_start: usize,
        hash_code: u32,
        data_index: usize,
    ) {
        debug_assert!((data_index as u32) < self.mask);
        if let Err(empty_index) = self.find_entry(data, data, block_start, hash_code)
            && let Some(slot) = self.table.get_mut(empty_index)
        {
            *slot = (hash_code << self.shift) | ((data_index as u32) + 1);
        }
    }

    fn find_entry<A: BlockElem, B: BlockElem>(
        &self,
        data: &[A],
        block_data: &[B],
        block_start: usize,
        hash_code: u32,
    ) -> Result<usize, usize> {
        let shifted_hash_code = hash_code << self.shift;
        let initial_entry_index = ((hash_code % (self.length as u32 - 1)) as usize) + 1;
        let mut entry_index = initial_entry_index;
        loop {
            let entry = self.table.get(entry_index).copied().unwrap_or(0);
            if entry == 0 {
                return Err(entry_index);
            }
            if (entry & !self.mask) == shifted_hash_code {
                let data_index = ((entry & self.mask) - 1) as usize;
                if equal_blocks(
                    data.get(data_index..).unwrap_or(&[]),
                    block_data.get(block_start..).unwrap_or(&[]),
                    self.block_length,
                ) {
                    return Ok(entry_index);
                }
            }
            entry_index = self.next_index(initial_entry_index, entry_index);
        }
    }

    fn find_entry_value(
        &self,
        data: &[u32],
        block_value: u32,
        hash_code: u32,
    ) -> Result<usize, usize> {
        let shifted_hash_code = hash_code << self.shift;
        let initial_entry_index = ((hash_code % (self.length as u32 - 1)) as usize) + 1;
        let mut entry_index = initial_entry_index;
        loop {
            let entry = self.table.get(entry_index).copied().unwrap_or(0);
            if entry == 0 {
                return Err(entry_index);
            }
            if (entry & !self.mask) == shifted_hash_code {
                let data_index = ((entry & self.mask) - 1) as usize;
                if all_values_same_as(
                    data.get(data_index..).unwrap_or(&[]),
                    self.block_length,
                    block_value,
                ) {
                    return Ok(entry_index);
                }
            }
            entry_index = self.next_index(initial_entry_index, entry_index);
        }
    }

    #[inline]
    fn next_index(&self, initial_entry_index: usize, entry_index: usize) -> usize {
        (entry_index + initial_entry_index) % self.length
    }
}

#[derive(Debug)]
struct MutableCodePointTrie {
    index: Vec<u32>,
    index3_null_offset: i32,
    data: Vec<u32>,
    data_null_offset: i32,
    initial_value: u32,
    error_value: u32,
    high_start: u32,
    high_value: u32,
    index16: Vec<u16>,
    flags: Vec<u8>,
}

impl MutableCodePointTrie {
    fn new(initial_value: u32, error_value: u32) -> Self {
        Self {
            index: vec![0; I_LIMIT],
            index3_null_offset: -1,
            data: Vec::with_capacity(INITIAL_DATA_LENGTH),
            data_null_offset: -1,
            initial_value,
            error_value,
            high_start: 0,
            high_value: initial_value,
            index16: Vec::new(),
            flags: vec![0; I_LIMIT],
        }
    }

    fn get(&self, c: u32) -> u32 {
        if c > MAX_UNICODE {
            return self.error_value;
        }
        if c >= self.high_start {
            return self.high_value;
        }
        let i = (c as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        if self.flags.get(i) == Some(&ALL_SAME) {
            self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(self.initial_value)
        } else {
            let block = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
            self.data
                .get(block + ((c as usize) & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK))
                .copied()
                .unwrap_or(self.initial_value)
        }
    }

    fn ensure_high_start(&mut self, c: u32) {
        if c >= self.high_start {
            // Round up to a UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY boundary to simplify compaction.
            let c = (c + UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY as u32)
                & !(UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY as u32 - 1);
            let i = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
            let i_limit = (c as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
            if let Some(flags) = self.flags.get_mut(i..i_limit) {
                flags.fill(ALL_SAME);
            }
            if let Some(index) = self.index.get_mut(i..i_limit) {
                index.fill(self.initial_value);
            }
            self.high_start = c;
        }
    }

    fn alloc_data_block(&mut self, block_length: usize) -> usize {
        let new_block = self.data.len();
        self.data.resize(new_block + block_length, 0);
        new_block
    }

    fn get_data_block(&mut self, i: usize) -> usize {
        if self.flags.get(i) == Some(&MIXED) {
            return self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
        }
        if i < BMP_I_LIMIT {
            let mut new_block = self.alloc_data_block(UCPTRIE_FAST_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH);
            let mut i_start = i & !(SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK - 1);
            let i_limit = i_start + SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK;
            while i_start < i_limit {
                debug_assert_eq!(self.flags.get(i_start), Some(&ALL_SAME));
                let val = self.index.get(i_start).copied().unwrap_or(0);
                if let Some(slice) = self
                    .data
                    .get_mut(new_block..new_block + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH)
                {
                    slice.fill(val);
                }
                if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i_start) {
                    *f = MIXED;
                }
                if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i_start) {
                    *idx = new_block as u32;
                }
                i_start += 1;
                new_block += UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
            }
            self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize
        } else {
            let new_block = self.alloc_data_block(UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH);
            let val = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0);
            if let Some(slice) = self
                .data
                .get_mut(new_block..new_block + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH)
            {
                slice.fill(val);
            }
            if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                *f = MIXED;
            }
            if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                *idx = new_block as u32;
            }
            new_block
        }
    }

    fn set(&mut self, c: u32, value: u32) {
        if c > MAX_UNICODE {
            return;
        }
        self.ensure_high_start(c);
        let block = self.get_data_block((c as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);
        if let Some(slot) = self
            .data
            .get_mut(block + ((c as usize) & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK))
        {
            *slot = value;
        }
    }

    fn set_range(&mut self, start: u32, end: u32, value: u32) {
        if start > MAX_UNICODE || end > MAX_UNICODE || start > end {
            return;
        }
        self.ensure_high_start(end);

        let mut start = start as usize;
        let mut limit = (end as usize) + 1;
        if (start & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK) != 0 {
            // Set partial block at [start..following block boundary[.
            let block = self.get_data_block(start >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);
            let next_start = (start + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK) & !UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK;
            if next_start <= limit {
                if let Some(slice) = self.data.get_mut(
                    block + (start & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK)
                        ..block + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH,
                ) {
                    slice.fill(value);
                }
                start = next_start;
            } else {
                if let Some(slice) = self.data.get_mut(
                    block + (start & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK)
                        ..block + (limit & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK),
                ) {
                    slice.fill(value);
                }
                return;
            }
        }

        // Number of positions in the last, partial block.
        let rest = limit & UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK;

        // Round down limit to a block boundary.
        limit &= !UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_MASK;

        // Iterate over all-value blocks.
        while start < limit {
            let i = start >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
            if self.flags.get(i) == Some(&ALL_SAME) {
                if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                    *idx = value;
                }
            } else {
                let block = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
                if let Some(slice) = self
                    .data
                    .get_mut(block..block + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH)
                {
                    slice.fill(value);
                }
            }
            start += UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        }

        if rest > 0 {
            // Set partial block at [last block boundary..limit[.
            let block = self.get_data_block(start >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);
            if let Some(slice) = self.data.get_mut(block..block + rest) {
                slice.fill(value);
            }
        }
    }

    fn mask_values(&mut self, mask: u32) {
        self.initial_value &= mask;
        self.error_value &= mask;
        self.high_value &= mask;
        let i_limit = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        for (flag, idx) in self.flags.iter().zip(&mut self.index).take(i_limit) {
            if *flag == ALL_SAME {
                *idx &= mask;
            }
        }
        for d in &mut self.data {
            *d &= mask;
        }
    }

    fn find_high_start(&self) -> u32 {
        let mut i = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        while i > 0 {
            i -= 1;
            let match_high = if self.flags.get(i) == Some(&ALL_SAME) {
                self.index.get(i) == Some(&self.high_value)
            } else {
                let block = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
                let p = self.data.get(block..).unwrap_or(&[]);
                all_values_same_as(p, UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH, self.high_value)
            };
            if !match_high {
                return ((i + 1) << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3) as u32;
            }
        }
        0
    }

    fn compact_whole_data_blocks(
        &mut self,
        fast_i_limit: usize,
        all_same_blocks: &mut AllSameBlocks,
    ) -> usize {
        // ASCII data will be stored as a linear table, even if the following code
        // does not yet count it that way.
        let mut new_data_capacity = ASCII_LIMIT;
        // Add room for a small data null block in case it would match the start of
        // a fast data block where dataNullOffset must not be set in that case.
        new_data_capacity += UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        // Add room for special values (errorValue, highValue) and padding.
        new_data_capacity += 4;
        let i_limit = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        let mut block_length = UCPTRIE_FAST_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        let mut inc = SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK;
        let mut i = 0;
        while i < i_limit {
            if i == fast_i_limit {
                block_length = UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                inc = 1;
            }
            let mut value = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0);
            if self.flags.get(i) == Some(&MIXED) {
                // Really mixed?
                if let Some((&first, rest)) = self
                    .data
                    .get(value as usize..)
                    .and_then(|s| s.split_first())
                {
                    value = first;
                    if all_values_same_as(rest, block_length - 1, value) {
                        if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                            *f = ALL_SAME;
                        }
                        if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                            *idx = value;
                        }
                        // Fall through to ALL_SAME handling.
                    } else {
                        new_data_capacity += block_length;
                        i += inc;
                        continue;
                    }
                }
            } else {
                debug_assert_eq!(self.flags.get(i), Some(&ALL_SAME));
                if inc > 1 {
                    // Do all of the fast-range data block's ALL_SAME parts have the same value?
                    let all_same = self
                        .index
                        .get(i + 1..i + inc)
                        .is_some_and(|s| s.iter().all(|&x| x == value));
                    if !all_same {
                        // Turn it into a MIXED block.
                        self.get_data_block(i);
                        new_data_capacity += block_length;
                        i += inc;
                        continue;
                    }
                }
            }
            // Is there another ALL_SAME block with the same value?
            let other = match all_same_blocks.find_or_add(i, inc, value) {
                FindOrAddResult::Found(idx) => Some(idx),
                FindOrAddResult::NewUnique => None,
                FindOrAddResult::Overflow => {
                    // The fixed-size array overflowed. Slow check for a duplicate block.
                    let mut j_inc = SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK;
                    let mut j = 0;
                    let mut found = None;
                    loop {
                        if j == i {
                            all_same_blocks.add(i, inc, value);
                            break;
                        }
                        if j == fast_i_limit {
                            j_inc = 1;
                        }
                        if self.flags.get(j) == Some(&ALL_SAME) && self.index.get(j) == Some(&value)
                        {
                            all_same_blocks.add(j, j_inc + inc, value);
                            found = Some(j);
                            break;
                        }
                        j += j_inc;
                    }
                    found
                }
            };
            if let Some(other_idx) = other {
                if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                    *f = SAME_AS;
                }
                if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                    *idx = other_idx as u32;
                }
            } else {
                // New unique same-value block.
                new_data_capacity += block_length;
            }
            i += inc;
        }
        new_data_capacity
    }

    fn compact_data(
        &mut self,
        fast_i_limit: usize,
        new_data: &mut [u32],
        new_data_capacity: usize,
        data_null_index: Option<usize>,
        mixed_blocks: &mut MixedBlocks,
    ) -> usize {
        // The linear ASCII data has been copied into newData already.
        let mut new_data_length = 0;
        for idx in self
            .index
            .iter_mut()
            .take(ASCII_I_LIMIT)
            .step_by(SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK)
        {
            *idx = new_data_length as u32;
            new_data_length += UCPTRIE_FAST_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        }

        let mut block_length = UCPTRIE_FAST_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        mixed_blocks.init(new_data_capacity, block_length);
        mixed_blocks.extend(new_data, 0, 0, new_data_length);

        let i_limit = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        let mut inc = SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK;
        let mut fast_length = 0;
        let mut i = ASCII_I_LIMIT;
        while i < i_limit {
            if i == fast_i_limit {
                block_length = UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                inc = 1;
                fast_length = new_data_length;
                mixed_blocks.init(new_data_capacity, block_length);
                mixed_blocks.extend(new_data, 0, 0, new_data_length);
            }
            let flag = self.flags.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(ALL_SAME);
            if flag == ALL_SAME {
                let value = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0);
                // Find an earlier part of the data array of length blockLength
                // that is filled with this value.
                let mut n = mixed_blocks.find_all_same_block(new_data, value);
                // If we find a match, and the current block is the data null block,
                // and it is not a fast block but matches the start of a fast block,
                // then we need to continue looking.
                while let Some(n_val) = n {
                    if data_null_index == Some(i)
                        && i >= fast_i_limit
                        && n_val < fast_length
                        && is_start_of_some_fast_block(n_val as u32, &self.index, fast_i_limit)
                    {
                        n = find_all_same_block(
                            new_data,
                            n_val + 1,
                            new_data_length,
                            value,
                            block_length,
                        );
                    } else {
                        break;
                    }
                }
                if let Some(n_val) = n {
                    if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                        *idx = n_val as u32;
                    }
                } else {
                    let overlap =
                        get_all_same_overlap(new_data, new_data_length, value, block_length);
                    if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                        *idx = (new_data_length - overlap) as u32;
                    }
                    let prev_data_length = new_data_length;
                    let fill_len = block_length - overlap;
                    if let Some(slice) =
                        new_data.get_mut(new_data_length..new_data_length + fill_len)
                    {
                        slice.fill(value);
                    }
                    new_data_length += fill_len;
                    mixed_blocks.extend(new_data, 0, prev_data_length, new_data_length);
                }
            } else if flag == MIXED {
                let block_offset = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
                let block = self.data.get(block_offset..).unwrap_or(&[]);
                if let Some(n_val) = mixed_blocks.find_block(new_data, block, 0) {
                    if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                        *idx = n_val as u32;
                    }
                } else {
                    let overlap = get_overlap(new_data, new_data_length, block, 0, block_length);
                    if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                        *idx = (new_data_length - overlap) as u32;
                    }
                    let prev_data_length = new_data_length;
                    let copy_len = block_length - overlap;
                    if let (Some(dst), Some(src)) = (
                        new_data.get_mut(new_data_length..new_data_length + copy_len),
                        block.get(overlap..block_length),
                    ) {
                        dst.copy_from_slice(src);
                    }
                    new_data_length += copy_len;
                    mixed_blocks.extend(new_data, 0, prev_data_length, new_data_length);
                }
            } else {
                // SAME_AS
                let j = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
                let same_idx = self.index.get(j).copied().unwrap_or(0);
                if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                    *idx = same_idx;
                }
            }
            i += inc;
        }

        new_data_length
    }

    fn compact_index(&mut self, fast_i_limit: usize, mixed_blocks: &mut MixedBlocks) -> usize {
        let fast_index_length = fast_i_limit >> (UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT - UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);
        if ((self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_FAST_SHIFT) <= fast_index_length {
            // Only the linear fast index, no multi-stage index tables.
            self.index3_null_offset = UCPTRIE_NO_INDEX3_NULL_OFFSET;
            return fast_index_length;
        }

        // Condense the fast index table.
        // Also, does it contain an index-3 block with all dataNullOffset?
        let mut fast_index = [0u16; UCPTRIE_BMP_INDEX_LENGTH];
        let mut i3_first_null: i32 = -1;
        for (j, ([first, rest @ ..], fast_slot)) in self
            .index
            .get_mut(..fast_i_limit)
            .unwrap_or(&mut [])
            .as_chunks_mut::<SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK>()
            .0
            .iter_mut()
            .zip(&mut fast_index)
            .enumerate()
        {
            let mut i3 = *first;
            *fast_slot = i3 as u16;
            if i3 == self.data_null_offset as u32 {
                if i3_first_null < 0 {
                    i3_first_null = j as i32;
                } else if self.index3_null_offset < 0
                    && (j as i32 - i3_first_null + 1) == UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH as i32
                {
                    self.index3_null_offset = i3_first_null;
                }
            } else {
                i3_first_null = -1;
            }
            // Set the index entries that compactData() skipped.
            // Needed when the multi-stage index covers the fast index range as well.
            for slot in rest {
                i3 += UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH as u32;
                *slot = i3;
            }
        }

        mixed_blocks.init(fast_index_length, UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH);
        mixed_blocks.extend(&fast_index, 0, 0, fast_index_length);

        // Examine index-3 blocks.
        let mut index3_capacity = 0;
        i3_first_null = self.index3_null_offset;
        let mut has_long_i3_blocks = false;
        let i_start = if fast_i_limit < BMP_I_LIMIT {
            0
        } else {
            BMP_I_LIMIT
        };
        let i_limit = (self.high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
        for i in (i_start..i_limit).step_by(UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH) {
            let mut ored_i3 = 0;
            let mut is_null = true;
            for &i3 in self
                .index
                .get(i..i + UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH)
                .unwrap_or(&[])
            {
                ored_i3 |= i3;
                if i3 != self.data_null_offset as u32 {
                    is_null = false;
                }
            }
            if is_null {
                if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                    *f = I3_NULL;
                }
                if i3_first_null < 0 {
                    if ored_i3 <= 0xffff {
                        index3_capacity += UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                    } else {
                        index3_capacity += INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                        has_long_i3_blocks = true;
                    }
                    i3_first_null = 0;
                }
            } else if ored_i3 <= 0xffff {
                if let Some(n) = mixed_blocks.find_block(&fast_index, &self.index, i) {
                    if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                        *f = I3_BMP;
                    }
                    if let Some(idx) = self.index.get_mut(i) {
                        *idx = n as u32;
                    }
                } else {
                    if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                        *f = I3_16;
                    }
                    index3_capacity += UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                }
            } else {
                if let Some(f) = self.flags.get_mut(i) {
                    *f = I3_18;
                }
                index3_capacity += INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                has_long_i3_blocks = true;
            }
        }

        let index2_capacity = (i_limit - i_start) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2_3;

        // Length of the index-1 table, rounded up.
        let index1_length = (index2_capacity + UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_MASK) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_1_2;

        // Index table: Fast index, index-1, index-3, index-2.
        // +1 for possible index table padding.
        let index16_capacity =
            fast_index_length + index1_length + index3_capacity + index2_capacity + 1;
        self.index16.clear();
        self.index16.reserve(index16_capacity);
        self.index16
            .extend_from_slice(fast_index.get(..fast_index_length).unwrap_or(&[]));
        self.index16.resize(index16_capacity, 0);

        mixed_blocks.init(index16_capacity, UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH);
        let mut long_i3_blocks = MixedBlocks::new();
        if has_long_i3_blocks {
            long_i3_blocks.init(index16_capacity, INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH);
        }

        // Compact the index-3 table and write an uncompacted version of the index-2 table.
        let mut index2 = [0u16; UNICODE_LIMIT >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_2];
        let mut i2_length = 0;
        i3_first_null = self.index3_null_offset;
        let index3_start = fast_index_length + index1_length;
        let mut index_length = index3_start;
        for i in (i_start..i_limit).step_by(UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH) {
            let i3: usize;
            let mut f = self.flags.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(I3_NULL);
            if f == I3_NULL && i3_first_null < 0 {
                // First index-3 null block. Write & overlap it like a normal block, then remember it.
                f = if self.data_null_offset <= 0xffff {
                    I3_16
                } else {
                    I3_18
                };
                i3_first_null = 0;
            }
            if f == I3_NULL {
                i3 = self.index3_null_offset as usize;
            } else if f == I3_BMP {
                i3 = self.index.get(i).copied().unwrap_or(0) as usize;
            } else if f == I3_16 {
                if let Some(n) = mixed_blocks.find_block(&self.index16, &self.index, i) {
                    i3 = n;
                } else {
                    let n = if index_length == index3_start {
                        // No overlap at the boundary between the index-1 and index-3 tables.
                        0
                    } else {
                        get_overlap(
                            &self.index16,
                            index_length,
                            &self.index,
                            i,
                            UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH,
                        )
                    };
                    i3 = index_length - n;
                    let prev_index_length = index_length;
                    let copy_len = UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH - n;
                    if let (Some(dst), Some(src)) = (
                        self.index16.get_mut(index_length..index_length + copy_len),
                        self.index.get(i + n..i + UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH),
                    ) {
                        for (d, &s) in dst.iter_mut().zip(src) {
                            *d = s as u16;
                        }
                    }
                    index_length += copy_len;
                    mixed_blocks.extend(
                        &self.index16,
                        index3_start,
                        prev_index_length,
                        index_length,
                    );
                    if has_long_i3_blocks {
                        long_i3_blocks.extend(
                            &self.index16,
                            index3_start,
                            prev_index_length,
                            index_length,
                        );
                    }
                }
            } else {
                debug_assert_eq!(f, I3_18);
                debug_assert!(has_long_i3_blocks);
                // Encode an index-3 block that contains one or more data indexes exceeding 16 bits.
                if let (Some(src_block), Some(dst_block)) = (
                    self.index.get(i..i + UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH),
                    self.index16
                        .get_mut(index_length..index_length + INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH),
                ) {
                    for (src8, [upper_slot, dst8 @ ..]) in src_block
                        .as_chunks::<8>()
                        .0
                        .iter()
                        .zip(dst_block.as_chunks_mut::<9>().0)
                    {
                        let mut upper_bits = 0u32;
                        for (&v, slot) in src8.iter().zip(dst8) {
                            upper_bits = (upper_bits << 2) | ((v & 0x30000) >> 16);
                            *slot = v as u16;
                        }
                        *upper_slot = upper_bits as u16;
                    }
                }
                if let Some(n) =
                    long_i3_blocks.find_block(&self.index16, &self.index16, index_length)
                {
                    i3 = n | 0x8000;
                } else {
                    let n = if index_length == index3_start {
                        // No overlap at the boundary between the index-1 and index-3 tables.
                        0
                    } else {
                        get_overlap(
                            &self.index16,
                            index_length,
                            &self.index16,
                            index_length,
                            INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH,
                        )
                    };
                    i3 = (index_length - n) | 0x8000;
                    let prev_index_length = index_length;
                    if n > 0 {
                        let start = index_length;
                        let copy_len = INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH - n;
                        self.index16
                            .copy_within(start + n..start + INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH, start);
                        index_length += copy_len;
                    } else {
                        index_length += INDEX_3_18BIT_BLOCK_LENGTH;
                    }
                    mixed_blocks.extend(
                        &self.index16,
                        index3_start,
                        prev_index_length,
                        index_length,
                    );
                    if has_long_i3_blocks {
                        long_i3_blocks.extend(
                            &self.index16,
                            index3_start,
                            prev_index_length,
                            index_length,
                        );
                    }
                }
            }
            if self.index3_null_offset < 0 && i3_first_null >= 0 {
                self.index3_null_offset = i3 as i32;
            }
            // Set the index-2 table entry.
            if let Some(slot) = index2.get_mut(i2_length) {
                *slot = i3 as u16;
            }
            i2_length += 1;
        }
        debug_assert_eq!(i2_length, index2_capacity);
        debug_assert!(index_length <= index3_start + index3_capacity);

        if self.index3_null_offset < 0 {
            self.index3_null_offset = UCPTRIE_NO_INDEX3_NULL_OFFSET;
        }
        assert!(
            index_length < (UCPTRIE_NO_INDEX3_NULL_OFFSET as usize) + UCPTRIE_INDEX_3_BLOCK_LENGTH,
            "The index-3 offsets exceed 15 bits"
        );

        // Compact the index-2 table and write the index-1 table.
        let mut block_length = UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_BLOCK_LENGTH;
        let mut i1 = fast_index_length;
        let mut i = 0;
        while i < i2_length {
            let n = if (i2_length - i) >= block_length {
                // normal block
                debug_assert_eq!(block_length, UCPTRIE_INDEX_2_BLOCK_LENGTH);
                mixed_blocks.find_block(&self.index16, &index2, i)
            } else {
                // highStart is inside the last index-2 block. Shorten it.
                block_length = i2_length - i;
                find_same_block(
                    &self.index16,
                    index3_start,
                    index_length,
                    &index2,
                    i,
                    block_length,
                )
            };
            let i2 = if let Some(n_val) = n {
                n_val
            } else {
                let overlap = if index_length == index3_start {
                    // No overlap at the boundary between the index-1 and index-3/2 tables.
                    0
                } else {
                    get_overlap(&self.index16, index_length, &index2, i, block_length)
                };
                let i2_val = index_length - overlap;
                let prev_index_length = index_length;
                let copy_len = block_length - overlap;
                if let (Some(dst), Some(src)) = (
                    self.index16.get_mut(index_length..index_length + copy_len),
                    index2.get(i + overlap..i + block_length),
                ) {
                    dst.copy_from_slice(src);
                }
                index_length += copy_len;
                mixed_blocks.extend(&self.index16, index3_start, prev_index_length, index_length);
                i2_val
            };
            // Set the index-1 table entry.
            if let Some(slot) = self.index16.get_mut(i1) {
                *slot = i2 as u16;
            }
            i1 += 1;
            i += block_length;
        }
        debug_assert_eq!(i1, index3_start);
        debug_assert!(index_length <= index16_capacity);

        index_length
    }

    fn compact_trie(&mut self, fast_i_limit: usize) -> usize {
        // Find the real highStart and round it up.
        debug_assert_eq!(
            self.high_start & (UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY as u32 - 1),
            0
        );
        self.high_value = self.get(MAX_UNICODE);
        let mut real_high_start = self.find_high_start();
        real_high_start = (real_high_start + (UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY as u32 - 1))
            & !(UCPTRIE_CP_PER_INDEX_2_ENTRY as u32 - 1);
        if real_high_start == UNICODE_LIMIT as u32 {
            self.high_value = self.initial_value;
        }

        // We always store indexes and data values for the fast range.
        // Pin highStart to the top of that range while building.
        let fast_limit = (fast_i_limit << UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3) as u32;
        if real_high_start < fast_limit {
            let start_i = (real_high_start as usize) >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3;
            if let Some(flags) = self.flags.get_mut(start_i..fast_i_limit) {
                flags.fill(ALL_SAME);
            }
            if let Some(index) = self.index.get_mut(start_i..fast_i_limit) {
                index.fill(self.high_value);
            }
            self.high_start = fast_limit;
        } else {
            self.high_start = real_high_start;
        }

        let mut new_data = Vec::with_capacity(ASCII_LIMIT);
        new_data.extend((0..ASCII_LIMIT as u32).map(|c| self.get(c)));

        // First we look for which data blocks have the same value repeated over the whole block,
        // deduplicate such blocks, find a good null data block (for faster enumeration),
        // and get an upper bound for the necessary data array length.
        let mut all_same_blocks = AllSameBlocks::new();
        let new_data_capacity = self.compact_whole_data_blocks(fast_i_limit, &mut all_same_blocks);
        new_data.resize(new_data_capacity, 0);

        let data_null_index = all_same_blocks.find_most_used();

        let mut mixed_blocks = MixedBlocks::new();
        let new_data_length = self.compact_data(
            fast_i_limit,
            &mut new_data,
            new_data_capacity,
            data_null_index,
            &mut mixed_blocks,
        );
        debug_assert!(new_data_length <= new_data_capacity);
        new_data.truncate(new_data_length);
        self.data = new_data;
        assert!(
            self.data.len() <= 0x3ffff + UCPTRIE_SMALL_DATA_BLOCK_LENGTH,
            "The offset of the last data block is too high to be stored in the index table"
        );

        if let Some(null_idx) = data_null_index
            && let Some(&offset) = self.index.get(null_idx)
            && let Some(&val) = self.data.get(offset as usize)
        {
            self.data_null_offset = offset as i32;
            self.initial_value = val;
        } else {
            self.data_null_offset = UCPTRIE_NO_DATA_NULL_OFFSET;
        }

        let index_length = self.compact_index(fast_i_limit, &mut mixed_blocks);
        self.high_start = real_high_start;
        index_length
    }

    fn build<T: TrieValue>(mut self, trie_type: TrieType) -> CodePointTrie<'static, T> {
        // The mutable trie always stores 32-bit values.
        // When we build a UCPTrie for a smaller value width, we first mask off unused bits
        // before compacting the data.
        match size_of::<T::ULE>() {
            1 => self.mask_values(0xff),   // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_8
            2 => self.mask_values(0xffff), // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_16
            3 | 4 => {}                    // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_32
            _ => {
                const {
                    assert!(matches!(size_of::<T::ULE>(), 1..=4));
                }
            }
        }

        let fast_limit = match trie_type {
            TrieType::Fast => BMP_LIMIT,
            TrieType::Small => UCPTRIE_SMALL_LIMIT,
        };
        let mut index_length = self.compact_trie(fast_limit >> UCPTRIE_SHIFT_3);

        // Ensure data table alignment: The index length must be even for uint32_t data.
        if size_of::<T::ULE>() > 2 && (index_length & 1) != 0 {
            if let Some(slot) = self.index16.get_mut(index_length) {
                *slot = 0xffee; // arbitrary value
            }
            index_length += 1;
        }

        // Make the total trie structure length a multiple of 4 bytes by padding the data table,
        // and store special values as the last two data values.
        let length = index_length * 2;
        if size_of::<T::ULE>() == 1 {
            // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_8
            let mut and3 = (length + self.data.len()) & 3;
            if and3 == 0 && self.data.ends_with(&[self.high_value, self.error_value]) {
                // all set
            } else if and3 == 3 && self.data.last() == Some(&self.high_value) {
                self.data.push(self.error_value);
            } else {
                while and3 != 2 {
                    self.data.push(self.high_value);
                    and3 = (and3 + 1) & 3;
                }
                self.data.push(self.high_value);
                self.data.push(self.error_value);
            }
        } else if size_of::<T::ULE>() == 2 {
            // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_16
            if ((index_length ^ self.data.len()) & 1) != 0 {
                // padding
                self.data.push(self.error_value);
            }
            if !self.data.ends_with(&[self.high_value, self.error_value]) {
                self.data.push(self.high_value);
                self.data.push(self.error_value);
            }
        } else {
            // UCPTRIE_VALUE_BITS_32
            // 32-bit data words never need padding to a multiple of 4 bytes.
            if !self.data.ends_with(&[self.high_value, self.error_value]) {
                if self.data.last() != Some(&self.high_value) {
                    self.data.push(self.high_value);
                }
                self.data.push(self.error_value);
            }
        }

        let header = CodePointTrieHeader {
            high_start: self.high_start,
            shifted12_high_start: ((self.high_start + 0xfff) >> 12) as u16,
            index3_null_offset: self.index3_null_offset as u16,
            data_null_offset: self.data_null_offset as u32,
            null_value: self.initial_value,
            trie_type,
        };

        let index_vec: ZeroVec<'static, u16> = if (self.high_start as usize) <= fast_limit {
            self.index
                .iter()
                .step_by(SMALL_DATA_BLOCKS_PER_BMP_BLOCK)
                .take(index_length)
                .map(|&idx| idx as u16)
                .collect()
        } else {
            self.index16.truncate(index_length);
            ZeroVec::alloc_from_slice(&self.index16)
        };

        let data_vec: ZeroVec<'static, T> = self
            .data
            .iter()
            .map(|&v| {
                #[expect(clippy::unwrap_used)] // values in `self.data` originated from `T::to_u32`
                T::try_from_u32(v).ok().unwrap()
            })
            .collect();

        #[expect(clippy::unwrap_used)]
        // `header`, `index_vec`, and `data_vec` are valid by construction
        CodePointTrie::try_new(header, index_vec, data_vec).unwrap()
    }
}
